# Figma Mobile NP PDP — UI law (legacy / earlier JMS frame)

> **If replicating the handcrafted mweb NP PLOT (`FINALL` / `46:9766`), use `figma-mweb-np-plot-ui` instead — that SoT wins.**  
> This file remains for older 360 JMS experiments only when the user explicitly points at that frame.

## 1. Section cards — NOT rounded

| Prop | Required (mobile) |
|---|---|
| Outer section radius | **`radius/none` (0)** — flat edges |
| Fill | `surface/white` |
| Left / right padding | **16px** = `spacing/m` |
| Top / bottom padding | **16px** = `spacing/m` (match L/R unless a measured SoT says otherwise) |
| Gap between content inside section | **16px** = `spacing/m` |
| Body stack gap (between sections) | **8px** = `spacing/xs` |

**Hard ban:** Do not apply `radius/2xl` / 24 on **outer** mobile section shells (web-only).  
**Hard ban:** Do not use **24** L/R pad inside mobile sections — always **16**.  
**Hard ban:** Do not use **16/24** gap *between* mobile sections — always **8**.

Nested chips / list panels / EMI pills may still use small radii (`radius/xs`–`radius/l`). First-fold summary shelf may keep **top-only** radius for hero overlap — body sections must stay flat. Summary L/R pad and internal gap also **16**.

## 1b. Summary badges (above project title)

Place **above** the project heading in the **summary shelf — never on the hero**.

### Zero brokerage — soft web `badge/base` SoT

Selected web First fold `badge/base`:

| Prop | Required |
|---|---|
| Fill | **`surface/default`** — soft; **never** black / `warm_neutral/800` / inverse |
| Label | Google Sans Flex **Regular 14** / **`text/secondary`** |
| Pad | **[4, 8, 4, 8]** |
| Radius | **`radius/xs` (4)** |
| Stroke | none |

### RERA — success verified pill (do not soften to badge/base)

| Prop | Required |
|---|---|
| Fill | **`semantic_surface/success`** |
| Label | Medium **12** / **`semantic_text/success`** |
| Leading icon | Bricks Iconography **`SealCheck`** 16 Fill, tint **`semantic_icons/success`** — never custom/CDN SVG |
| Pad | **[4, 8, 4, 8]** |
| Gap | **4** |
| Radius | **`radius/xs` (4)** |

### Row

| Prop | Required |
|---|---|
| Name | `Summary tags` |
| Layout | HORIZONTAL, gap **12** (`spacing/s`) |
| Order | before Title row |

### Hard bans

- Do **not** use black / inverse pills for Zero brokerage
- Do **not** restyle RERA into soft `badge/base` / `surface/default`
- Do **not** put these badges on the hero gallery

## 1c. Payment plan section (mobile)

Replace list-of-stages with a **scannable EMI card + CTA** (Housing PDP pattern):

| Layer | Recipe |
|---|---|
| Section shell | Flat, pad **16**, gap **16**, `surface/white` |
| Title | SemiBold **16** / `text/primary` |
| Card | `surface/subtle`, radius **`radius/l` (16)**, pad **16**, gap **12** |
| EMI line | Regular **14** / `text/primary`; amount span **SemiBold** (e.g. `₹1.11L`) |
| Meta | `Duration:` / `Interest:` labels Regular **12** `text/muted`; values Medium **12** `text/primary`; separator · |
| Breakup link | Medium **14** / `text/brand` + Bricks **chevron right** tinted `icon/brand_1` |
| CTA | Full-width **48**h, `surface/brand`, Medium **14** / `text/inverse`, radius **`radius/m`** |

**Hard ban:** Do not leave Payment plan as a raw stage amount list as the primary UI.

Every FAQ **question** row must show a trailing arrow so users know items expand/collapse.

| Prop | Required |
|---|---|
| Layout | HORIZONTAL, SPACE_BETWEEN / CENTER |
| Question | Medium **14** / `text/primary` (FILL) |
| Arrow | Iconography — Bricks **`CaretDown`** (prefer Size=16, key `a074229f2dfb5224e13da2152007a2f384739b97`) |
| Icon color | `icon/grey_1` |
| Collapsed | answer hidden; caret points down |
| Expanded | answer visible; caret may rotate to up (`CaretUp` / Chevron Up) if showing state |

**Hard ban:** FAQ questions as bare TEXT with no arrow.

## 3. Typography — mobile scale

| Role | Max / target | Token |
|---|---|---|
| Absolute max any text | **20px** | `font_size/2xl` |
| Section titles | **16** max — **never 18** | `font_size/lg` |
| Body / paragraphs | **14** — **not 16** | `font_size/m` |
| Meta / captions | **12** | `font_size/s` |
| CTA labels | **14** Medium | `font_size/m` |
| Price hero | ≤ **20** SemiBold | `font_size/2xl` |

Family: **Google Sans Flex** only.

**Hard bans:**
- Any text **> 20px** on mobile NP PDP
- Section headings at **18px** (`font_size/xl`) — too large; use **16**
- Body copy at **16px** (`font_size/lg`) — too large for body; use **14** (headings may use 16)

## 4. Hero gallery

| Prop | Required (mobile) |
|---|---|
| Hero / gallery image height | **430px** FIXED |
| Width | **360** (full bleed) |
| Overlays allowed | **Icons only** — Back / Share / Save (`figma-button-chrome` Recipe A) |
| Gallery icon stroke | **`border/default` · 1.5px** · INSIDE |
| Scroll cue | **Centre-aligned pagination dots** in the **media safe zone** (above summary overlap — see `figma-overlap-safe-zones`) |

**Hard bans on hero:**
- Do **not** put status **chips/pills** (RERA, Under construction, etc.) on the hero image
- Do **not** put **thumbnail strips** / “more images” previews on the hero
- Do **not** shrink hero below **430** without updating this rule
- Do **not** pin dots in the summary overlap band (they will be invisible / clipped)
- Do **not** use gallery icon stroke other than **1.5px** `border/default`

**Dots placement math:**
```
overlapDepth = abs(firstFold.itemSpacing) when negative  // e.g. 28
dots.bottom ≤ heroHeight - overlapDepth - spacing/m(16)
dots centred horizontally on 360
```

## 5. Chrome (unchanged)

Back / Share / Save / WhatsApp / Contact → `figma-button-chrome` (mobile recipes). Never circles.

## Verify before shipping mobile UI

```
Outer sections: radius === 0 (token none)
Section pad L/R === 16 (spacing/m); gap between content === 16
Body gap between sections === 8 (spacing/xs)
Hero gallery height === 430
Hero: no pills/thumbs; has centre Gallery dots; icons only
Gallery icons: strokeWeight === 1.5, stroke === border/default
Summary badges: Zero brokerage = soft badge/base; RERA = success + SealCheck (do not soften RERA)
No TEXT fontSize > 20
Section headings ≤ 16 (never 18)
No body paragraph at 16
Each FAQ question row has CaretDown (or Up when expanded)
```

